<title>JAPAN: TABLE-Japan May revised industrial output up 4.5%.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Japan May revised industrial output up 4.5%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in May rose a revised 4.5 percent from the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 3.8 percent increase, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On a year-on-year basis, industrial production increased a revised 7.5 percent, against a preliminary estimate of a 6.8 percent increase.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  May    PRELIM    MONTH AGO MayINDEX</p>
<p> Output		 +4.5    +3.8    -0.5     105.2</p>
<p> Shipments	    +4.0    +3.8    -2.8     105.6</p>
<p> Inventories	  +2.1    +1.9    +3.1    108.7</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>  Shipments ratio   -1.7    -2.2    +8.0    112.8</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>			  May     PRELIM    MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output		 +7.5    +6.8    +4.8</p>
<p> Shipments	    +6.9    +6.7    +4.4</p>
<p> Inventories	  -0.6    -0.8    -2.2</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>  Shipments ratio   -3.2    -3.7    -1.9</p>
</text>
